      "problem": "Given the linear transformation $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}0x+0y \\\\ 0x+0y\\end{aligned}],$ find  $2\\cdot \\text{nullity}(T)-4.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write down the standard matrix of $T:$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(T)).$ Notice that $T$ has $2$ non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore, $\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(T))=2.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n2\\cdot \\text{nullity}(T)-4=2\\cdot 2-4=0.\n$$",
